      // [LOCAL-PATCH] On LocalStack we want SimpleAWSCredentialsProvider, which
      // reads the test/test creds we set via --conf spark.hadoop.fs.s3a.access.key
      // / secret.key. The upstream DefaultAWSCredentialsProviderChain walks env →
      // sysprops → STS → EC2 IMDS → ECS metadata; on a developer laptop those
      // can return real-AWS-shaped creds and route requests to real AWS, masking
      // every LocalStack-targeted operation behind a 403. In QA/prod this branch
      // is dead code and behaviour is identical to the upstream chain.
      .config("spark.hadoop.fs.s3a.aws.credentials.provider", if (sys.env.contains("AWS_ENDPOINT_URL")) "org.apache.hadoop.fs.s3a.SimpleAWSCredentialsProvider" else "com.amazonaws.auth.DefaultAWSCredentialsProviderChain")
